# Inactive-attribute WebGL test enters the shared harness through its script dependencies

Firefox repository `git:314d8065c5ad68c7e5c5f92d`, revision `1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b`. Scope: DOM Canvas WebGL conformance tests and the shared Mochitest harness. Languages in the cited files: HTML. File roles are listed in the metadata. No production WebGL implementation is claimed.

The inspected inactive-attribute target loads js-test-pre and two WebGL helper scripts, creates its description/console/canvas nodes, creates a WebGL2 context, invokes the attribute-aliasing helper for two shader sources, sets successfullyParsed=true, and directly loads js-test-post. This proves one concrete entry into the shared harness.

## State and ownership

The test owns `canvas`, `gl`, `glFragmentShader`, and `successfullyParsed` in its document. The helper calls consume the WebGL context, fragment shader, and two distinct vertex shader source elements. Their internal assertions and WebGL resource cleanup were not followed.

**Scope limit:** The helper bodies and GPU implementation are not analyzed here; this record does not claim the target test passed or complete behavior coverage.

## Evidence

[`dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/conformance2/attribs/gl-bindAttribLocation-aliasing-inactive.html` — `script and DOM dependencies`, lines 10–19](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/conformance2/attribs/gl-bindAttribLocation-aliasing-inactive.html#L10-L19). Exact excerpt from lines 11–13:

```html
<script src="../../js/js-test-pre.js"></script>
<script src="../../js/webgl-test-utils.js"></script>
<script src="../../js/tests/gl-bindattriblocation-aliasing.js"></script>
```

[`dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/conformance2/attribs/gl-bindAttribLocation-aliasing-inactive.html` — `test execution and direct postlude`, lines 36–53](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/conformance2/attribs/gl-bindAttribLocation-aliasing-inactive.html#L36-L53). Exact excerpt from lines 39–53:

```html
var wtu = WebGLTestUtils;
var canvas = document.getElementById("canvas");
var gl = wtu.create3DContext(canvas, {antialias: false}, 2);
var glFragmentShader = wtu.loadShader(gl, wtu.simpleColorFragmentShaderESSL300, gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER);

debug("Testing with shader that has statically used but inactive attributes.");
runBindAttribLocationAliasingTest(wtu, gl, glFragmentShader, wtu.getScript('vertexShaderStaticallyUsedButInactive'));

debug("");
debug("Testing with shader that has entirely unused attributes.");
runBindAttribLocationAliasingTest(wtu, gl, glFragmentShader, wtu.getScript('vertexShaderUnused'));

var successfullyParsed = true;
</script>
<script src="../../js/js-test-post.js"></script>
```

## Test links and validation

**Execution-only:** This target executes the shared helper and postlude route. The attribute helper assertions were not read here, so no direct assertion link for its detailed behavior is claimed.

The cited implementation, callers, and applicable receiver bodies were read. An independent source review accepted this scoped relationship with its listed gaps. No Firefox or Thunderbird product tests, generator run, or build ran for this evidence. There is no runtime pass/fail result. No Thunderbird–Firefox call chain is added by this Firefox-only slice.

